mode: "100644"
text: "# Workflows, checklists & worked examples\n\n## The weekly social-set workflow (repeatable loop)\nBrand Kit locked → pick/adapt ONE master layout per format (quote card, carousel, promo) → swap all stock for\nbrand imagery → Magic Resize to the platform set → QA at thumb-size → export → scheduling-and-queue → WoopSocial.\nBoring on purpose: the repeatable loop is what makes six platform versions still look like one campaign.\n\n## The Bulk Create pattern (the leverage move)\n1. Build ONE master template; mark the variable fields (headline, tip text, price, image).\n2. Prepare the CSV/Excel — one row per asset; image URLs if imagery varies.\n3. Connect fields → generate all variants in one run.\n4. QA pass: text overflow, widows, line breaks, contrast on every variant.\nUse for: tip series, product cards, stat cards, event speaker cards, localized sets (pair with Magic Switch).\n\n## The de-templating checklist (kill the \"Canva look\")\nStock imagery replaced with yours ✓ · layout bones changed (something moved/merged/deleted) ✓ · Brand Kit fonts +\ncolors applied over defaults ✓ · template decorations stripped ✓ · a stranger can't name the template ✓ ·\nconsistent with your other posts (the system, not the template, is the consistency) ✓.\n\n## Legibility floor (before any export)\n≤2 fonts · WCAG contrast · min readable sizes at thumb-scale · text never over busy imagery without a\npanel/overlay · safe zones respected per platform · alt text drafted.\n\n## Worked example A — \"Blunt indie founder\" (Bulk Create)\n\"had 52 pricing myths in a spreadsheet. built one black card template, wired 3 fields, bulk-created all 52 in\nabout 20 minutes. qa caught 4 overflows. a year of tuesday posts done before lunch. the feature's been sitting\nin canva the whole time — i just never clicked it.\" — one master, CSV, QA pass, honest time math.\n\n## Worked example B — \"Warm bookkeeping studio\" (de-templating)\n\"We loved a template — and that was the problem, because three competitors clearly loved it too. So we kept its\nspacing, swapped every photo for our own desk-and-receipts shots, set our serif over the default font, and\ndeleted the swooshes. Same bones, finally our face. One small step: replace just the photos this week — it does\nmore than you'd think.\" — scaffolding kept, look replaced, one small step.\n\n## Never\nSkip the Brand Kit and prompt \"in my brand colors\" every time · ship the untouched template · rip a premium\ntemplate from a screenshot · strip stock watermarks / evade licenses · impersonate another brand's look/logo ·\ntrust a blog's credit numbers over the in-app tracker · let Magic Write's first draft be the voice · claim\nWoopSocial generates or edits designs · skip the human review of a visual.\n"
